A||||3||MCordray||86 to 88 Duke Swap||||1||
Z||000000||MCordray||02-17-2000||11:41 PM||||Can an '88 4 cyl. Duke be put into an '86 that originally came with a Duke? In other words, are the 84-88 Iron Dukes interchangeable?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ozzy||02-18-2000||01:01 AM||||If you swap the ECM out as well. The '87 &'88 were DIS motors with a crank sensor. The earlier models had distributors. The '88 also had a serpentine belt instead of a normal fan belt. If you have a donor car it would be easier I should think.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||02-18-2000||08:19 AM||||You just about have to use the donor car engine wiring harness too. The 87 and 88 2.5 engines are unique due to them being DIS and also the eletronic fuel injection is totally different from the earlier models. You can't just swap manifolds, because the newer engine doesn't have a distributor. There might be a way to adapt something, but why bother with that hassle.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||02-18-2000||10:04 AM||||This is as complex a change as putting in a V6 would be. The 87+ motors with DIS are very diferant from the distributor motors.<P>All the wiring needs changing.<BR>The fuel lines need changing nearly all the way to the tank.<BR>The Throtle and TV cables are diferant.<BR>The ECM and harness are completely diferant.<BR>Cruise control adds even more problems. Cruise is an ECM main board function on 87+. It was a sub board/module prior to that.<P>About all it will do is bolt up to the existing mounts and the bell housing.||||reg||1
